{"id":"29f5643a-a812-4201-bed1-e8d1e59e000f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2b0c697957eb6f54","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/bablr.ts","baseline":{"blob":"39c191c4a47a74ad21e11cc2467ff5c5a9a9a805","start":9195,"end":9233},"shape":{"type":"MemberExpression","atoms":["vscode",".","workspace",".","onDidSaveTextDocument"]},"context":{"before":"c03144397fd6594b","after":"7cd517e1e9300f1d"}},"payload":{"text":"(a file whose warning shows is parsed again as it's saved: it goes when it parses)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:01.263Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:10:01.263Z"}
{"id":"31419212-cb8b-444e-9ffc-ca1835d7c45f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/bablr.ts","baseline":{"blob":"99b00cbaa3f9c8f4d7d491d24e0aa5a9f90abd11","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"Which files BABLR parses, and a warning on each one it can't (*Unparsable files flagged*): nothing can attach to code\nBABLR can't parse — no note, no runtime evidence — so a file it can't take is said in Problems, with why, until it\nparses again. And how much of a folder it takes, for the rewrite's Measure (ARCHITECTURE.md, *Comments become\nnotes*: what of the scope BABLR parses is measured first).\n\n- the command `editor.bablr.check` (\"BABLR: Check Which Files Parse…\"): a folder's code files parsed one at a time,\nwith a progress notification to cancel it by, the ones BABLR can't take in Problems, and what it took said;\n- `bablr.check` { path, exclude? }: the same, for agents' `code_parses`, with each file it can't parse and why.\n\nAnd a text with its comments blanked (`stripped`), for the code alone (git-refs.ts' `.refs/<name>~stripped/`).\n\nAnd what's placed on code stays on it: `editor.annotations.spans`, `.refer` and `.resolve`, for anything an extension attaches to\ncode (editor-api's annotations.ts is their contract; RUNTIME-EVIDENCE.md, *Durable annotations on spans*). A reference not\nfound by its own id is looked for further: followed from the commit or text it was made against, and in the other changed files.\n\nBABLR runs in its own worker (workers/bablr-worker.ts), started the first time it's asked — not at boot: it's a big\nbundle — and asked one text at a time, each kept by its blob oid there, so a file is parsed once. A file whose warning\nshows is parsed again as it's saved.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:16.386Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:16.386Z"}
{"id":"3ef44dfb-1f54-499b-9970-322be9d159a4","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ebea221892e22219","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/bablr.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7efd2bcfc00d5f6c6c18908435b65faf57c0a362","start":2076,"end":2133},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","CODE_FILES","=","\"","**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts,js,jsx,mjs,cjs}","\""]},"context":{"before":"a4ffce90c45e9dcb","after":"a9b8c5eca640360d"}},"payload":{"text":"The files BABLR's grammar may take.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:11.996Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:11:11.996Z"}
